  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\nPR #2828 truncates its opposite-orientation five-b gap tables at three calls per outer label and four calls in total. This package supplies an explicit coverage certificate for those caps, including pure-dirty calls whose active projection is zero.\n\nA separate 2+3 meet-in-the-middle implementation reconstructs all **5,664 compatible active profile pairs**. Rank demand in the other gaps proves the 3/4 caps. Literal 3\u00d73 matrix calculations reconstruct both orientations' bounded operator tables: **81,935 states representing 2,798,629 words per orientation**. The optional comparison matches the complete profile set and every table entry/multiplicity against #2828 at 8a1000c09819b43ca9a8f2929788af4af40dab70.\n\nOnly research/ut4-five-b-coverage-audit/ is added. This is a scoped coverage/operator audit. It does not independently certify the remaining dirty-prefix filters, final whole-word rejection, inherited arbitrary-workspace compression, or a native supplier/new \u03ba.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\nCard: bit-new-register-model, changed to a complementary audit because the pending #2828 already supplies the requested construction-bound work. TASK.json records the selection, scope change and bottleneck connection.\n\nStarted from main b5e86d8104338796ce3cdf71666b6dbe72ec17fa; refreshed and rebased onto canonical main 23ef28cbeb7a3e2e985be22cab6832424bd98cf6 at 2026-10-16 01:18:45 UTC. Relevant instructions and scientific inputs were unchanged. Live PR searches found #2828 as the audit object; Discussion coverage remains incomplete and no advance claim was posted.\n\n## Validation\n\nPython 3.12.14 on Windows; standard library only. The independent replay imports no predecessor code.\n\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/ut4-five-b-coverage-audit\npython3.12 -B research/ut4-five-b-coverage-audit/compare_reference.py REFERENCE_ROOT\n```\n\nThe second command is optional and requires the pinned reference export.\n\n- Registered replay passed in 71.954 seconds; metadata and source pins passed.\n- All 5,664 profiles passed direct degree-1\u20133 subsequence expansion of the fourteen retained quotient equations.\n- Controls detect a changed middle coupling, unjustified smaller caps, lost pure-dirty contributions and reversed contraction order.\n- The optional comparison matched the exact profile set and gap tables while preserving every original census output.\n- The author's original verifier and controls also passed. Those reruns are not independent implementations.\n\nThe README documents exact-source export instructions, canonical digests and unrun obligations. No selected supplier cold replay or frontier change is claimed.\n\n## Credit\n\nThe full exclusion belongs to steph4n-gh's #2828, building on Gareth Davidson (#2027/#2314/#2343), Nick Petalas (#2175), ToikY (#1662/#1680), CinnaDavis (#1541), and Aaron Wang's profile method (#1690). No predecessor code is vendored. New work is Apache-2.0.\n\nPrepared with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; no independent human review or subagents.\n\n## Open next questions\n\nIndependently reconstruct the remaining dirty-prefix equations and final AC/ACB/BAC rejection for all fifteen-call five-b splits. Start from the then-current pinned #2828 head and reuse these profile/gap digests. This would audit the remaining computational implication; the inherited workspace-compression proof needs separate review. No computational blocker is known. See the [README and scoped handoff](https://github.com/josecarlosgonzalezroque-design/integer-mult-bounds/blob/f46783ec06f184612e7859f575cbdad2ea722a4f/research/ut4-five-b-coverage-audit/README.md#open-next-questions).",
